From e567d669e629a4309b377c1bff2e66d6f38aad57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 02:53:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remember VM/server passwords for later lookup, cover more
 Azure regions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two user-reported issues, both about the server detail screen:

1. "покажи в разделе сервера пароль тоже, чтобы если забыли они могли
   посмотреть" -- neither Azure nor UpCloud ever return the generated
   admin/root password again after creation (it's write-only at the API
   level), so once the one-time success screen scrolled away there was
   no way to recover it. cloud_store now has set_vm_secret/get_vm_secret/
   remove_vm_secret, keyed by account + VM name (Azure) or server UUID
   (UpCloud). The password is stored right after a successful password-
   auth creation (skipped entirely for SSH-key auth, since there's no
   password), shown in the detail screen at every place it's rendered
   (view, start/stop/restart, reimage, plan-change), and the stored copy
   is deleted when the VM/server itself is deleted so it doesn't linger
   forever.

2. A live user's VM in "denmarkeast" showed a plain globe instead of a
   flag on the detail screen -- _AZURE_REGION_COUNTRY only covered a
   curated subset of regions. Expanded it to essentially the full real
   Azure region catalog (including Gov/DoD, EUAP canary, and several
   newer regions: Denmark, Greece, Taiwan, etc.) so the globe fallback
   should now be rare.

Covered by new assertions in test_azure_handlers.py (remembered password
shown in VM detail, cleaned up on delete, "denmarkeast" resolves to a
real flag) and test_cloud_handlers.py (same password remember/cleanup
for UpCloud). Full regression suite re-run clean.

